{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The assembly.</b> Some say this heh is for calling. In my opinion there is no sign of calling in the sacred language — the proof is 'the four and the one,' among them משה משה. Rather, this heh is the heh of knowledge, and the sign of calling is not." "<b>As you, as the stranger.</b> I have already explained the rule of the letters kaf-pa-yod-nun when they combine."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the four and the one' is obscure; it may refer to four (or five) instances cited by his opponents as counterexamples. Rendered hyper-literally without expansion. The phrase משה משה is quoted from biblical theophany formulae.", 1 "'The letters kaf-pa-yod-nun' refers to the inseparable prepositions and conjunction (כפל מן של) treated as a group; the identity of 'pa' (פ) as peh is inferred from context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:49.877039183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}